<title>NORWAY: Statoil seals 12-month oil tanker charter.</title>
<headline>Statoil seals 12-month oil tanker charter.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said on Thursday it had chartered the tanker Nordic Torinita for 12 months from owners Ugland/Nordic American Shipping.</p>
<p>Statoil said it had chartered the vessel primarily to ship the group's own cargoes of North Sea oil to northwest Europe and North America. The 108,000-tonner also will be used for oil shipments undertaken by Statoil for others, the company's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>The vessel can carry 732,000 barrels of oil and has a double hull.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
